          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Sebastien Buisson",
          "email": "sbuisson@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-02 14:17:00.000000000",
          "tz": 60
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Sebastien Buisson",
          "email": "sbuisson@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-26 08:36:46.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20974 target: drop SEC_CTX_INIT_CONT opcode",
        "message": "LU-20974 target: drop SEC_CTX_INIT_CONT opcode\n\nSEC_CTX_INIT_CONT (802) is the RPC opcode that would carry a\nPTLRPC_GSS_PROC_CONTINUE_INIT request. No Lustre client has ever\nsent it, and with the multi-round GSS negotiation removed it has\nno purpose left.\n\nRemove it:\n- drop the SEC_CTX_INIT_CONT handler entries from the MDT and\n  common target handler tables, and from the unconnected-export\n  and recovery checks in tgt_handler.c, so the opcode is now\n  rejected as unsupported;\n- comment out SEC_CTX_INIT_CONT in enum sec_cmd, keeping 802\n  reserved, and drop it from wirecheck/wiretest;\n- keep the positional 802 row in ll_rpc_opcode_table, by number;\n- remove the unused OBD_FAIL_SEC_CTX_INIT_CONT_NET fail_loc and\n  the tgt_sec_ctx_init_cont() prototype, which had no definition.\n\nFixes: d2d56f38da01 (\"make HEAD from b_post_cmd3\")\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-1\nTest-Parameters: testgroup=review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-2\nTest-Parameters: kerberos=true testlist=sanity-krb5\nSigned-off-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I9d74aab34645685ce933195e315e0633194eebf7\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
